--- a/packages/settings-ui/README.md
+++ b/packages/settings-ui/README.md
@@ -18,11 +18,21 @@ Settings panel frame and standard sections for Right Suite apps: appearance, upd
 | `@rightkit/settings-ui/appearance` | `appearanceSection`, `AppearanceOptions`. Needs `@rightkit/react-shell` and `@rightkit/theme`, not `@rightkit/license`. Pair with `/core` in an app without licensing (0.5.0). |
 | `@rightkit/settings-ui/standard` | `standardSections`, the section factories, `useLicenseSection`, `useDoctor`. Needs the optional peers below. |
 | `@rightkit/settings-ui/headless` | The search state as hooks and no-DOM providers, for a host with its own markup: `SettingsSearchProvider`, `useSettingsSearch`, `useSettingsRow`, `useSettingsItem`, `useSettingsHit`, `useSettingsGroup`, `useSettingsSection`, `useSettingsSearchField`, `useSettingsSearchStatus`, `useSearchKeys`, `highlightText`, `parseSearchTerms`, `defaultAnnouncement`, `SettingsGroupScope`, `SettingsSectionScope`. Imports only `react`; no stylesheet. See [Headless search](#headless-search). |
+| `@rightkit/settings-ui/unstyled` | Unstyled slot variants for an app with its own markup: `SettingsFrame`, `UpdatesView`, `updateStatusText`, `LegalLinksView`, `AboutView`, `DiagnosticsView` and their prop types. Controlled by props; every part takes `classNames` and the larger ones `slots`. Imports only `react`. |
 | `@rightkit/settings-ui/settings.css` | Stylesheet |
 | `@rightkit/settings-ui/shell-adapter` | `createShellBackends` (settings, models and secrets backends) and the engine wire constants `METHODS` and `EVENTS` for `rightkit-app-settings` / `rightkit-models`, over the `@rightkit/tauri-shell` engine bridge. The engine is described structurally, so this subpath needs no import of `@rightkit/tauri-shell`. |
 
 The persistence port is the `SettingsBackend` interface (`load`, `patch` with `expectedRevision`, optional `subscribe`). Use the shell adapter in a Tauri app, or implement the interface over your own store. For example, a blob-backed adapter keeps the whole settings object in one JSON string, bumps a revision on each patch and throws `code: "revision_conflict"` on a stale write. `useSettings(backend)` takes any `SettingsBackend`. `createMemorySettings` is the in-memory reference implementation. The root and `/core` also export `createMemorySecrets` (an in-memory `SecretsBackend`), `RevisionConflict`, and `createShellBackends`, `METHODS` and `EVENTS` as deprecated re-exports of `/shell-adapter`.
 
+## Added in 0.7.0
+
+- `SelectBox` and `PathPicker` (`/core`): a native select and a read-only path with Change and Clear. `PathPicker` calls an injected `pick()`; the package imports no dialog plugin.
+- `SettingsModal` (`/core`): the panel as a modal with a draft model (dirty banner, Reload / Discard / Save footer, "Discard unsaved changes?" close guard, `pending` lock, focus trap, `#settings=<id>` deep link). Helpers `parseSettingsHash` and `formatSettingsHash`.
+- `SettingRow` `proGate`: Pro badge, locked control, reason and Upgrade button. `IndexProgress`: one-line index progress with a bar.
+- `modelsSection`: `disabled` (all or per model, with a reason), `disabledNote`, `showStatus` and `statusLabels` (install state visible while the feature is off), and an `actions` slot per row.
+- `doctorSection`: `probe` (one shared report) and `notes` (render from the report). `diagnosticsSection`: `logTail` (multi-file tail preview with Reveal).
+- `@rightkit/settings-ui/unstyled`: `SettingsFrame`, `UpdatesView`, `LegalLinksView`, `AboutView`, `DiagnosticsView` with no styling, for an app with its own markup.
+
 ## Peer dependencies
 
 | Peer | Range | Note |
